@C.COMP
Syntax: C.Comp [<opts>] <file>
Usage : C compiler single pass front end - assembler source in one step
Opts  :
  -o=<file>  write output to <file> (default: standard output)
  -s         strip symbol information from the output
  -p         emit profiling information
Note  : does the work of c.pass1 and c.pass2 together and is driven by
        CC2.  It needs more free memory than the two pass path, so on
        small systems compile with CC1 instead.
